---
import PlaygroundShell from '../../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Place pods, then kill a node" hint="A scheduler filters out the nodes where a pod does not fit, then scores the rest. Change the scoring rule and see utilisation, stranded capacity and pods that cannot be placed. Then kill the busiest node and pick the heartbeat grace period: a short one reschedules quickly but evicts healthy nodes on a slow network.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>Start with the defaults: <b>80 pods, first-fit, kill the busiest node, congested network, 20 s grace</b>. All 80 pods fit, with <b>86% of the CPU</b> and 80% of the memory requested, but <b>98 GB of memory is stranded</b> on nodes with no CPU left. Then node 3 (32 CPUs) dies, its <b>15 pods</b> are evicted, and with no spare room <b>12 stay Pending</b>. Pods are back (or stuck) about <b>24 s</b> after the failure, but this network produces <b>646 false evictions</b> an hour.</li>
    <li>Switch the scoring to <b>spread</b>: the node death evicts only <b>11 pods</b> and <b>6</b> end up Pending, but spreading leaves <b>1 pod</b> unschedulable even before the failure. Switch to <b>balanced</b>: <b>0</b> unschedulable and only 3 CPU and 18 GB stranded, but node 3 now holds <b>19 pods</b>, so more are evicted. Raise the pods to <b>90</b>: balanced still places all 90, while the other rules leave 3 to 7 Pending.</li>
    <li>Raise the grace to <b>40 s</b> on the congested network: false evictions fall to <b>0</b> and pods come back after about <b>44 s</b> (worst case 58 s). Choose the <b>flaky</b> network and 40 s still gives <b>10</b> false evictions; it takes 60 s to make them <b>0</b>. A calm network is fine at 30 s. The timeout trades how fast a real failure is noticed against how often a slow heartbeat is mistaken for one.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg ocb" data-ocb>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Scoring rule <select class="pg-in" data-policy>
        <option value="first" selected>first-fit (first node that fits)</option>
        <option value="best">best-fit (least room left)</option>
        <option value="spread">spread (most room left)</option>
        <option value="balanced">balanced (even CPU and memory)</option>
      </select></label>
      <label>Pods to place <input type="range" min="50" max="100" step="5" value="80" data-pods /> <b data-podsval></b></label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" data-kill checked /> Kill the busiest node</label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Network <select class="pg-in" data-net>
        <option value="calm">calm</option>
        <option value="congested" selected>congested</option>
        <option value="flaky">flaky</option>
      </select></label>
      <label>Heartbeat grace (s) <input type="range" min="15" max="120" step="5" value="20" data-grace /> <b data-graceval></b></label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" data-b1><h3>Requested of the cluster</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o1></span><span class="pg-note" data-n1></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b2><h3>Unschedulable pods</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o2></span><span class="pg-note" data-n2></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b3><h3>Stranded capacity</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o3></span><span class="pg-note" data-n3></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b4><h3>Node failure</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o4></span><span class="pg-note" data-n4></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b5><h3>Time until pods run again</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o5></span><span class="pg-note" data-n5></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b6><h3>False evictions per hour</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o6></span><span class="pg-note" data-n6></span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-box"><h3>The 10 nodes <span class="pg-note">(after the failure, if you kill one)</span></h3><div class="ocb-nodes" data-nodes></div></div>
    <p class="pg-out" data-verdict aria-live="polite"></p>
    <p class="pg-note">Model: 10 nodes with 8, 16 or 32 CPUs and 4 GB of memory per CPU, and a fixed list of up to 100 pods that request 1 to 4 CPUs and 2 to 24 GB (a mix of small web pods, API pods, CPU-heavy jobs, caches and databases). Pods arrive in the same order each time. First-fit takes the first node in the list with room, best-fit the node left with the least room, spread the node with the most room left, and balanced the node whose CPU and memory use end up closest together. Stranded capacity is the CPU on nodes with under 2 GB of memory free, plus the memory on nodes with no whole CPU free: it exists, but no pod can use it. After the kill, the evicted pods go through the same scheduler again. Heartbeats are sent every 10 s. A node is wrongly evicted when two heartbeats arrive further apart than the grace period (200 healthy nodes for one hour: network delay, rare long stalls and lost heartbeats). Time until pods run again is the wait for the grace period to run out after the last heartbeat that arrived, plus 8 s to schedule, pull the image and start (the median and the worst of 200 simulated failures). Real clusters add a separate delay before evicting pods, which is 5 minutes by default.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<style is:global>
  .playground .ocb-nodes { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(8.5rem, 1fr)); gap: 8px; }
  .playground .ocb-node { border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px; padding: 6px 8px; background: var(--surface); display: grid; gap: 3px; font: .8rem var(--font-mono); }
  .playground .ocb-node.dead { border-style: dashed; color: var(--muted); }
  .playground .ocb-bar { height: 7px; border-radius: 4px; background: var(--surface-2); overflow: hidden; }
  .playground .ocb-bar > span { display: block; height: 100%; background: var(--accent); }
  .playground .ocb-bar.mem > span { background: var(--good); }
</style>
<script>
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-ocb]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = <T extends HTMLElement>(s: string) => root.querySelector<T>(s)!;
    // SIM-START
    type Pod = { id: number; cpu: number; mem: number };
    type Node = { capC: number; capM: number; cpu: number; mem: number; pods: Pod[]; dead: boolean };
    const SIZES = [8, 16, 32, 16, 8, 32, 16, 16, 8, 16]; const RESTART = 8; const HB = 10;
    const TYPES = [[1, 2, 0.3], [2, 4, 0.25], [4, 4, 0.15], [1, 16, 0.2], [4, 24, 0.1]];
    const SEED = 11; const POOL_SIZE = 100; const GB_PER_CPU = 4; // pods drawn; node memory per CPU
    const BEST_NORM = { cpu: 16, mem: 64 }; // best-fit scales leftover CPU and GB to a comparable size
    const SCORE_EPS = 1e-12; // ties keep the earlier node
    const MIN_POD = { cpu: 1, mem: 2 }; // smallest pod: free room below this is stranded
    const HB_SEED = 77; const MIN_DELAY_S = 0.05; const SPIKE = { min: 5, span: 20 }; // heartbeat delay floor; congestion spike seconds
    const HEALTHY_NODES = 200; const HB_COUNT = 360; // nodes and heartbeats (one hour) checked for false alarms
    const DEATHS = 200; const HB_LOOKBACK = 6; // simulated node deaths; heartbeats before the death that may still arrive
    const NO_HEARTBEAT = -1e9;
    const STRANDED_BAD = 60; const SLOW_RECOVERY_S = 45; // verdict thresholds
    let seed = SEED; const rnd = () => ((seed = (seed * 1664525 + 1013904223) % 4294967296) / 4294967296);
    const POOL: Pod[] = Array.from({ length: POOL_SIZE }, (_, id) => { let u = rnd(); let k = 0; while (k < TYPES.length - 1 && u >= TYPES[k][2]) { u -= TYPES[k][2]; k++; } return { id, cpu: TYPES[k][0], mem: TYPES[k][1] }; });
    const fresh = (): Node[] => SIZES.map((c) => ({ capC: c, capM: c * GB_PER_CPU, cpu: c, mem: c * GB_PER_CPU, pods: [], dead: false }));
    function score(p: Pod, policy: string, n: Node) {
      const fc = (n.cpu - p.cpu) / n.capC; const fm = (n.mem - p.mem) / n.capM;
      if (policy === 'best') return -((n.cpu - p.cpu) / BEST_NORM.cpu + (n.mem - p.mem) / BEST_NORM.mem);
      if (policy === 'spread') return fc + fm;
      if (policy === 'balanced') return -Math.abs(fc - fm);
      return 0;
    }
    // Filter: the nodes that are alive and have room. Score: pick the best of those. First-fit stops at the first one.
    function place(pods: Pod[], nodes: Node[], policy: string) {
      const pending: Pod[] = [];
      for (const p of pods) {
        let best = -1; let bs = -Infinity;
        for (let i = 0; i < nodes.length; i++) {
          const n = nodes[i]; if (n.dead || n.cpu < p.cpu || n.mem < p.mem) continue;
          if (policy === 'first') { best = i; break; }
          const s = score(p, policy, n); if (s > bs + SCORE_EPS) { bs = s; best = i; }
        }
        if (best < 0) pending.push(p); else { const n = nodes[best]; n.cpu -= p.cpu; n.mem -= p.mem; n.pods.push(p); }
      }
      return pending;
    }
    function stats(nodes: Node[]) {
      const live = nodes.filter((n) => !n.dead);
      const capC = live.reduce((s, n) => s + n.capC, 0); const capM = live.reduce((s, n) => s + n.capM, 0);
      return {
        cpuU: live.reduce((s, n) => s + n.capC - n.cpu, 0) / capC, memU: live.reduce((s, n) => s + n.capM - n.mem, 0) / capM,
        inUse: live.filter((n) => n.pods.length).length,
        strCpu: live.reduce((s, n) => s + (n.mem < MIN_POD.mem ? n.cpu : 0), 0), strMem: live.reduce((s, n) => s + (n.cpu < MIN_POD.cpu ? n.mem : 0), 0),
      };
    }
    const NET: Record<string, { m: number; sp: number; dr: number }> = { calm: { m: 0.1, sp: 0.0005, dr: 0.0005 }, congested: { m: 0.8, sp: 0.01, dr: 0.01 }, flaky: { m: 1.5, sp: 0.03, dr: 0.06 } };
    function heartbeats(net: string, grace: number) {
      const c = NET[net]; let s = HB_SEED; const r = () => ((s = (s * 1664525 + 1013904223) % 4294967296) / 4294967296);
      const delay = () => MIN_DELAY_S - c.m * Math.log(1 - r()) + (r() < c.sp ? SPIKE.min + r() * SPIKE.span : 0);
      let falseEv = 0; let flapping = 0;
      for (let n = 0; n < HEALTHY_NODES; n++) {
        const arr: number[] = [];
        for (let i = 0; i < HB_COUNT; i++) { const d = delay(); if (r() < c.dr) continue; arr.push(i * HB + d); }
        arr.sort((a, b) => a - b); let mine = 0;
        for (let i = 1; i < arr.length; i++) if (arr[i] - arr[i - 1] > grace) mine++;
        falseEv += mine; if (mine > 0) flapping++;
      }
      const res: number[] = [];
      for (let k = 0; k < DEATHS; k++) {
        const phase = r() * HB; let lastArr = NO_HEARTBEAT; // the node dies at time phase; heartbeat 0 was sent at time 0
        for (let i = -HB_LOOKBACK; i <= 0; i++) { const d = delay(); const dropped = r() < c.dr; if (!dropped) lastArr = Math.max(lastArr, i * HB + d); }
        res.push(Math.max(phase, lastArr + grace) - phase + RESTART);
      }
      res.sort((a, b) => a - b);
      return { falseEv, flapping, median: res[DEATHS / 2], worst: res[DEATHS - 1] };
    }
    function run(policy: string, podCount: number, kill: boolean) {
      const nodes = fresh(); const pods = POOL.slice(0, podCount);
      const pending = place(pods, nodes, policy); const before = stats(nodes);
      let killed = -1; let evicted = 0; let after = pending; let stuckEv = 0;
      if (kill) {
        killed = 0; nodes.forEach((n, i) => { if (n.pods.length > nodes[killed].pods.length) killed = i; });
        const gone = nodes[killed].pods; evicted = gone.length; nodes[killed].dead = true; nodes[killed].pods = [];
        after = place([...gone, ...pending], nodes, policy); const ids = new Set(gone.map((p) => p.id)); stuckEv = after.filter((p) => ids.has(p.id)).length;
      }
      return { nodes, pending, before, killed, evicted, after, stuckEv, perNode: before.inUse ? podCount / before.inUse : 0 };
    }
    // SIM-END
    const memo = new Map<string, ReturnType<typeof heartbeats>>();
    const hbFor = (net: string, g: number) => { const k = `${net}:${g}`; if (!memo.has(k)) memo.set(k, heartbeats(net, g)); return memo.get(k)!; };
    const nodeEls = SIZES.map((c, i) => {
      const d = document.createElement('div'); d.className = 'ocb-node';
      const t = document.createElement('span'); const cb = document.createElement('div'); cb.className = 'ocb-bar'; cb.append(document.createElement('span'));
      const mb = document.createElement('div'); mb.className = 'ocb-bar mem'; mb.append(document.createElement('span'));
      cb.title = `Node ${i + 1} CPU requested`; mb.title = `Node ${i + 1} memory requested`;
      d.append(t, cb, mb); q('[data-nodes]').append(d);
      return { d, t, cb: cb.firstElementChild as HTMLElement, mb: mb.firstElementChild as HTMLElement };
    });
    const fmt = (n: number) => Math.round(n).toLocaleString('en-US');
    const color = (id: string, c: string) => q<HTMLElement>(id).style.setProperty('--c', c);
    function draw() {
      const policy = q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-policy]').value; const podCount = Number(q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-pods]').value);
      const kill = q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-kill]').checked; const net = q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-net]').value; const grace = Number(q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-grace]').value);
      q('[data-podsval]').textContent = String(podCount); q('[data-graceval]').textContent = `${grace} s`;
      const r = run(policy, podCount, kill); const h = hbFor(net, grace);
      nodeEls.forEach((e, i) => {
        const n = r.nodes[i]; e.d.classList.toggle('dead', n.dead);
        e.t.textContent = n.dead ? `node ${i + 1}: DOWN` : `node ${i + 1}: ${n.pods.length} pods`;
        e.cb.style.width = `${((n.capC - n.cpu) / n.capC) * 100}%`; e.mb.style.width = `${((n.capM - n.mem) / n.capM) * 100}%`;
        e.d.setAttribute('aria-label', `Node ${i + 1}, ${n.capC} CPUs, ${n.dead ? 'down' : `${n.pods.length} pods, CPU ${Math.round(((n.capC - n.cpu) / n.capC) * 100)}% and memory ${Math.round(((n.capM - n.mem) / n.capM) * 100)}% requested`}`);
      });
      const b = r.before;
      q('[data-o1]').textContent = `CPU ${Math.round(b.cpuU * 100)}%, memory ${Math.round(b.memU * 100)}%`;
      q('[data-n1]').textContent = `${b.inUse} of ${SIZES.length} nodes in use before any failure`;
      q('[data-o2]').textContent = `${r.pending.length} of ${podCount}`;
      q('[data-n2]').textContent = r.pending.length ? 'Pending: every node was filtered out' : 'every pod found a node';
      q('[data-o3]').textContent = `${b.strCpu} CPU, ${b.strMem} GB`;
      q('[data-n3]').textContent = 'free, but on nodes that lack the other resource';
      if (kill) {
        q('[data-o4]').textContent = `node ${r.killed + 1} died: ${r.evicted} pods evicted`;
        q('[data-n4]').textContent = `${r.evicted - r.stuckEv} rescheduled, ${r.after.length} Pending now`;
      } else { q('[data-o4]').textContent = 'no failure'; q('[data-n4]').textContent = 'tick the box to kill the busiest node'; }
      q('[data-o5]').textContent = `${h.median.toFixed(0)} s typical, ${h.worst.toFixed(0)} s worst`;
      q('[data-n5]').textContent = `${grace} s grace + ${RESTART} s to start elsewhere, minus time since the last heartbeat`;
      q('[data-o6]').textContent = fmt(h.falseEv);
      q('[data-n6]').textContent = `${h.flapping} of ${HEALTHY_NODES} healthy nodes hit it; about ${fmt(h.falseEv * r.perNode)} needless pod restarts`;
      color('[data-b1]', 'var(--accent)');
      color('[data-b2]', r.pending.length ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--good)');
      color('[data-b3]', b.strCpu + b.strMem / GB_PER_CPU > STRANDED_BAD ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--accent)');
      color('[data-b4]', kill && r.after.length ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--accent)');
      color('[data-b5]', h.median > SLOW_RECOVERY_S ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--accent)');
      color('[data-b6]', h.falseEv > 0 ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--good)');
      const out = q('[data-verdict]'); const bad = r.pending.length > 0 || h.falseEv > 0 || (kill && r.after.length > 0); out.classList.toggle('bad', bad);
      const parts: string[] = [];
      parts.push(r.pending.length ? `${r.pending.length} pods cannot be placed, although ${b.strCpu} CPU and ${b.strMem} GB are free: the free room is in the wrong shape.` : `All ${podCount} pods are placed.`);
      if (kill) parts.push(r.stuckEv > 0 ? `After node ${r.killed + 1} dies, ${r.after.length} pods are Pending, since the other nodes have no room for all ${r.evicted} evicted pods.` : `The ${r.evicted} evicted pods all fit on the other nodes.`);
      parts.push(h.falseEv > 0 ? `A ${grace} s grace on a ${net} network wrongly evicts healthy nodes ${fmt(h.falseEv)} times an hour.` : `A ${grace} s grace gives no false evictions on a ${net} network, and a real failure costs about ${h.median.toFixed(0)} s.`);
      out.textContent = parts.join(' ');
    }
    let queued = false;
    const schedule = () => { if (queued) return; queued = true; requestAnimationFrame(() => { queued = false; draw(); }); };
    root.addEventListener('input', schedule); root.addEventListener('change', schedule);
    draw();
  });
</script>
